---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | ABOH LEGAL"
  description="Privacy Policy for ABOH LEGAL. How we collect, use, disclose, and protect your personal information under Alberta's Personal Information Protection Act."
>
  <Hero label="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" />

  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-20 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10">

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">ABOH LEGAL ("we", "us", "our") is the operating name of Prince Aboh Professional Corporation, a law firm at 4937 48 Avenue, St. Paul, Alberta T0A 3A4. This policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect personal information through this website (www.abohlegal.ca), our online booking page, and when you contact us. We handle personal information in accordance with Alberta's <em>Personal Information Protection Act</em> (PIPA) and our professional duty of confidentiality.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">2. Our Privacy Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">Prince Aboh, Barrister and Solicitor, is responsible for our privacy practices. He can answer your questions about how we collect, use, disclose, or store personal information, including through service providers outside Canada. Contact him at <a href="mailto:info@abohlegal.ca" class="text-gold underline hover:no-underline">info@abohlegal.ca</a>, at <a href="tel:+18254610107" class="text-gold underline hover:no-underline">(825) 461-0107</a>, or by mail at the address above.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">3. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-body-text leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address, location, the other party's name, the type of matter, and your message.</li>
          <li><strong>Online booking:</strong> your name, email address, the other party's name, the type of matter, the meeting type you choose, your phone number if you choose a phone call, any note about a safe way to reach you, and the time you book.</li>
          <li><strong>Email, phone, and text messages:</strong> what you choose to send or tell us. Calls and text messages to our office line are handled by our phone service and may be recorded or transcribed.</li>
          <li><strong>Website visits:</strong> our website host automatically receives technical information such as your IP address, browser type, and the pages you visit. It uses this to deliver and secure the website.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed mt-4">Before we confirm that we can act for you, please give us only what we need to check for conflicts of interest: your name, the other party's name, and the type of matter.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">We use your information to respond to you, to check for conflicts of interest, to decide whether we can help with your matter, to schedule and hold appointments, and to communicate with you. We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for marketing without your consent.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">5. Service Providers, Including Outside Canada</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">We use service providers to host this website, receive contact form messages, run our online booking page, and provide our email, phone, text messaging, and video meeting systems. Some of these providers are located outside Canada, mainly in the United States, so your information may be collected, used, or stored there.</p>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed mt-4">These providers may use your information only to provide their services to us. Information held outside Canada is subject to the laws of that country and may be accessible to its authorities. For written information about our policies and practices for service providers outside Canada, or with any questions about them, contact our privacy contact in section 2.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">6. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">This website does not use cookies for tracking or analytics. Services you use through links on this website, such as our online booking page, may set their own cookies under their own policies.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">7. Retention</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">We keep inquiry information as long as we need it to respond, to check for conflicts of interest, and to meet our legal and professional obligations. If we do not act for you, we keep only what we need for those purposes, and we protect it as confidential.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">8. Security</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">We use reasonable security measures to protect personal information from unauthorized access, collection, use, disclosure, copying, change, or destruction.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">9. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed mb-4">Under PIPA, you may:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-body-text leading-relaxed">
          <li>ask for access to your personal information that we hold, and for information about how we have used or disclosed it;</li>
          <li>ask us to correct an error or omission in your personal information; and</li>
          <li>withdraw or change your consent, on reasonable notice, subject to our legal and professional obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed mt-4">To make a request, contact our privacy contact in section 2. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the Office of the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Alberta.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">Our website is not directed at children under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information from minors through this website.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-navy text-lg md:text-xl font-bold mb-3">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-body-text leading-relaxed">We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with a new revision date.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 pt-4 border-t border-gray-200">Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
